course: dictionary
lesson: 616
title: Learning from context: the axolotl
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some animals have names that sound like they should mean something else, and context helps you find out what they are. «The axolotl is a salamander that never grows up» tells you it is an animal and not a fish, even though it lives in water and is called a «Mexican walking fish».
explain: Look at the clues around a word. «An axolotl hunts by suddenly opening its wide mouth and sucking in worms» shows that it catches and eats small creatures. Its smile is just the shape of its mouth, so the smile is not a real happy face.
explain: Phrases like «regrow a whole lost leg» give you more clues. Regrow means to grow again, so the axolotl can make new body parts after it loses them. Swap your meaning into the sentence: "can grow again a whole lost leg" makes sense, so your meaning fits.
fact: An axolotl is a Mexican salamander, a kind of amphibian.
fact: An axolotl keeps its baby features all its life, including feathery gills on its head and a tail fin.
fact: Gills are the feathery parts that let an animal breathe in water.
fact: An axolotl can regrow lost legs, tails, and even parts of its heart and brain.
fact: The name comes from the Aztec language Nahuatl, and wild axolotls are critically endangered.
exercise: «An axolotl is a salamander that never grows up.» What is an axolotl? | A plant that grows in the desert | A bird that cannot fly | A fish that lives in the sea | *A salamander that keeps its baby features all its life
exercise: The axolotl has feathery frills on its head. What are those frills called? | Fins | Lungs | Scales | *Gills
exercise: «Wild axolotls are critically endangered.» What does endangered mean? | *At risk of dying out | Found in every country | Very large and strong | Happy and well fed
test: «An axolotl can regrow a lost leg without leaving a scar.» What does regrow mean? | Break into pieces | Shrink smaller | *Grow again | Hide away
test: Why is the axolotl called a «Mexican walking fish» but not a fish? | It lives in the sea | It has scales | It walks on land | *It is an amphibian, a salamander, not a fish
exam: Which clue shows that the axolotl is a hunter? | *«Sucking in worms, insect larvae and small fish» | Its tail fin | Its pink gills | Its smile
